<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shanghai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shanghai is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s largest city, a port at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> on the Huangpu River. Opened to foreign trade by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanking</a> in 1842, it grew around foreign concessions into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>'s leading commercial and financial centre by the 1920s. It was the birthplace of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> in 1921, suffered Japanese attack in 1932 and 1937, and remains the country's economic capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shanghai.jpg" alt="Shanghai" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huangpu_Park_20124-Shanghai_(32208802494).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
